                                "sense_id": "6d15376f-f993-3bb7-9e64-369d94a96f96",
                                "text": "Pierrette et Jacquot"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "788a6ab0-6da9-318b-af99-b9b9cb1ee893",
                        "entry_id": "142356ea-6523-3156-99c8-223185faeff0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Souvent attribué au perroquet → voir jacquot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efb9b143-97d1-4057-b7ef-3490f0a36c39",
                                "sense_id": "788a6ab0-6da9-318b-af99-b9b9cb1ee893",
                                "text": "Il était placé auprès de la porte, et plusieurs s’étonnaient qu’il ne répondît pas au nom de Jacquot, puisque tous les perroquets s’appellent Jacquot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b660a2-65ed-4f63-a025-d2a7aa3aaee0",
                                "sense_id": "788a6ab0-6da9-318b-af99-b9b9cb1ee893",
                                "text": "Jacquot : histoire d’un illustre perroquet"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29d0db0c-6d74-4282-9998-d34fcd39bc42",
                        "source_entry_id": "142356ea-6523-3156-99c8-223185faeff0",
                        "target_lang_word": "Jamie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Jamie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c5885d3-dc8f-38c5-9e08-405bb5760445",
                                        "entry_id": "47f0cb7b-3c5e-380a-b0c7-e5590dcb9ff5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A unisex given name.",
                                            "A diminutive of the male given name James, from English and Scottish, also used as a formal given name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "427c4a5a-3377-4bb2-baf3-3ef681ec7c81",
                                                "sense_id": "5c5885d3-dc8f-38c5-9e08-405bb5760445",
                                                "text": "Primarily seen as a publicity vehicle for late-year releases, the awards show and its promoters have lately made pretensions to Oscar oracling: Jamie Foxx won the “breakthrough actor of the year” prize for “Ray” in 2004, after all, and Paul Haggis and his ensemble cast were honored for “Crash” four months before it won best picture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae953171-5914-4065-afdd-5133502c142e",
                                                "sense_id": "5c5885d3-dc8f-38c5-9e08-405bb5760445",
                                                "text": "\"Let's choose something simple. Children with simple names are never embarrassed with them. How about Jamie?\"\nMatthew looked doubtful. \"Jamie's fine,\" he said. \"But if he's called Jamie he's going to end up being a particular sort, if you know what I mean. He'll play rugby, he'll go to New Town bars after the international matches. Being called Jamie signs you up to an awful lot of Scottish upper-middle-class stuff.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bc1d4f9-895b-3d18-8800-ecbb20254c0c",
                                        "entry_id": "47f0cb7b-3c5e-380a-b0c7-e5590dcb9ff5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A unisex given name.",
                                            "A female given name from Hebrew derived from James, of modern American usage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86be87b0-ff37-35b7-8516-e7011e54ea62",
                                        "entry_id": "47f0cb7b-3c5e-380a-b0c7-e5590dcb9ff5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A unisex given name.",
                                            "Alternative form of Jaime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
